## 3. Cycle phase colours (the core of the app)

Each phase has a **fill** (ring segments, calendar dots, chart bars), a **tint** (chip, card and calendar-day background) and an **ink** (phase name text on the tint or on the page).

| Phase | Name | Fill | Tint light / dark | Ink light / dark | Feeling |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Menstrual | Merlot | `#6E1328` (dark `#B0304C`) | `#FFE6E7` / `#3A0F1A` | `#6E1328` / `#F4A3B0` | Rest, inward |
| Follicular | Peony | `#E07A8C` | `#FFE6E9` / `#3D1820` | `#7E3946` / `#FEA3B1` | Rising, curious |
| Ovulation | Champagne | `#D6B485` | `#FBF2E4` / `#2E2414` | `#6B5026` / `#EAD3AE` | Peak, social |
| Luteal | Mulberry | `#7E3A66` (dark `#A65A8C`) | `#FCE5F2` / `#2E1426` | `#7E3A66` / `#DBB3CA` | Settling, cozy |

Rules:
- Phase colours **only** mean a phase. Never use them for decoration, likes or generic buttons.
- Always show phases in order: menstrual → follicular → ovulation → luteal.
- Always write the phase name next to the colour. Peony and Champagne are light, so colour alone isn't enough.
- The "Today" card takes the **current phase's tint** as its background, with the phase ink for its text. This is the only large area where phase colour is used.
- The cycle ring is a donut chart with the four fills, with today's position marked.

---

## 4. Status colours

These are deliberately different from garnet, so an error never looks like a brand button. Always pair them with an icon and words.

| Status | Text / icon light | Tint light | Text dark | Tint dark | Example |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| success (sage) | `#2C5E45` | `#DDF3E6` | `#A9CAB7` | `#0F2A1D` | "Logged", goal reached |
| warning (amber) | `#774500` | `#FFE8D4` | `#EDB47C` | `#2E1A05` | "Period 2 days late", missing data |
| error (scarlet) | `#9E0008` | `#FFE7E3` | `#FEA69A` | `#3A0A08` | "Couldn't save", invalid input |
| info (dusk) | `#404F82` | `#E6EDFE` | `#B3C0E4` | `#141B33` | Tips, "Why this happens" science notes |

A late period is a *warning*, never an *error*. Keep the tone kind.

